# C4 Level 1 — System Context.  Render: d2 --theme 0 context.d2 context.svg
# Everything internal is hidden on purpose: this diagram exists to fix the system boundary.
direction: down

manager: Building manager {
  shape: person
}
occupant: Occupants {
  shape: person
}

sys: |md
  # Ventilation & climate control
  **[our system]**

  Senses CO₂, temperature and occupancy per room,
  decides ventilation and heating setpoints,
  and drives the actuators.
| {
  style.fill: "#dbeafe"
  style.stroke: "#2563eb"
  style.bold: true
}

buildsim: |md
  # BuildSim
  **[external, course-provided]**

  Shared building state: rooms, equipment,
  sensor values, actuator states, 3D viewer.
  Passive — no physics, no history, no decisions.
| {
  style.stroke-dash: 4
  style.fill: "#f3f4f6"
}

occupancysim: |md
  # occupancysim
  **[external, course-provided]**

  Generates the people and the simulated clock.
  Writes occupancy and entities to BuildSim.
| {
  style.stroke-dash: 4
  style.fill: "#f3f4f6"
}

manager -> sys: monitors decisions, room state and health [HTTP / Grafana]
manager -> buildsim: watches the 3D building [WebSocket, browser]
occupant -> occupancysim: are simulated as people\n(they never talk to the system)
occupancysim -> buildsim: PUT occupancy, entities [REST]
sys -> buildsim: reads occupancy + actuator state,\nwrites sensor values, actuator states,\nroom layers and alerts [REST]
sys -> occupancysim: reads the simulated clock [REST]
